On Wednesday 03 November 2010 17:25:59 Oren wrote:
> On Wed, Nov 3, 2010 at 16:42, Remo Dentato <rdentato@gmail.com> wrote:
> >> Will you stay at home tonight?
> >
> > {xu do stali le zdani ca le cabycte}
>
> Just for reference, would it be incorrect to use either { ti'u } or { ba }
> in place of { ca } here? Which way might be called most "lojbanic?"

"ti'u" and "de'i" are for the time when an appointment is set for, the date of 
a letter, and the like. I just got back from a meeting be ti'u li pabi, but I 
actually got there ca li pasopi'eji'icino. "ba le cabycte" means "after 
tonight".

Pierre
